import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Upwork Proposal Kit | Redefining Retirement"
  description="An easy way to dip your toe into freelancing and consulting after 50. Inside: a cover letter you can actually use, the messages I send once a client replies, a way to find adjacent work, and the prompt I'd paste into an agent today."
  type="article"
  noindex={true}
  bare={true}
>
<article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">

      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="issue-stamp">The Upwork Proposal Kit · Subscriber Edition</p>
        <h1 class="article-title">Upwork Proposal Kit: Proposals That Pop, updated for AI</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">An easy way to dip your toe into freelancing and consulting after 50. Set up your profile, find the right jobs, send a conversational cover letter, and reply like a pro. Now with the AI prompts I'd use for every step.</p>
        <p class="byline">By Corey Koehler · Redefining Retirement · Class of '90</p>
      </header>

      <div class="hello-section">
        <img
          src="/images/corey-portrait.jpg"
          alt="Corey Koehler"
          class="hello-photo"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
        <div class="hello-text">
          <h2>Hello</h2>
          <p>Thank you for grabbing this guide. Smart move!</p>
          <p>If you follow everything outlined below, you will be on your way to building your freelance business. It worked for me and a growing list of freelancers.</p>
          <p>I can't wait to hear how it works for you.</p>
          <p>I first wrote this as Proposals That Pop, before AI was part of the picture. The copy still works. What's new: in every section, I added how I'd use an AI agent like Grok Bot for that step today. I haven't written proposals with Grok Bot or any AI agent yet, so treat those parts as my plan, not my track record.</p>
          <p>Before we get started, I just want you to know that this guide is a work in progress. I am constantly looking to improve it. So, if you do not understand something, need a clarification or have an idea on how I could make something more clear, contact me here with the subject line: Proposals That Pop Question</p>
          <p>First, the thing some of you came for.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

