        <div class="prose">
          <h3>Look for adjacent work</h3>
          <p>Don't only search your exact skill. Search the tools around it.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Newsletters: newsletter writing, plus Mailchimp help or Beehiiv setup.</li>
            <li>HR: HR work, plus the HR platforms you actually used.</li>
            <li>Bookkeeping: bookkeeper jobs, plus QuickBooks or Xero help.</li>
            <li>Drafting: drafting work, plus SolidWorks or AutoCAD help.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>That last one is me. Years ago I helped an engineering department move from 2D AutoCAD to 3D SolidWorks. That still wins me work.</p>
          <h3>Don't shy away from teach-me jobs</h3>
          <p>Some clients want to be taught, not served. Most freelancers skip those. I wouldn't.</p>
          <p>Several clients hired me to teach them Google Ads by the hour. Once they saw the work involved, many asked me to just run it. My experience, not a promise.</p>
